- net
- pass
- mesa_foot

' The foot's desk. Every signature a world makes with a secret, other than
' its pages, is made here by the foot, when a record asks for it: a hand or
' a door writes an ask and never holds a key. An ask is a record beneath
' /<self>/io/mesa/ask that says what is wanted (want) and is not yet marked
' done. The foot answers each once, in one event: what was asked for is
' written, and the ask is marked done (1) with what it is told, or done (2)
' with why not.
'
' Three secrets are the foot's, kept as files of its own and never as
' records: the live seed that signs pages, the custody seed that signs this
' world's identity log, and a maker secret. From the maker secret come the
' secret of every invitation this world mints and the custody seed of every
' name it claims, so the two files are all there is to keep safe.
'
' Signatures are made before the world is asked to write anything. What the
' world is handed holds statements, letters and grants, which are public,
' and no secret.
+ desk
  + keys
    : live=nat custody=nat maker=nat
  + tag
    ' A number or a word as bytes.
    \ text=nat
    ^ nat
    | add text (bex (mul 8 (wid text)))
  + invitation
    ' The secret of the invitation this world mints under a number. It is
    ' derived whenever it is needed and is never written.
    \ k=desk/keys id=nat
    ^ nat
    | Blake3Keyed (Blake3Keyed k.maker (desk/tag "invite")) (desk/tag id)
  + claimed
    ' The custody seed this world holds for a name it claimed.
    \ k=desk/keys name=nat
    ^ nat
    | Blake3Keyed (Blake3Keyed k.maker (desk/tag "claimed")) (desk/tag name)
  + custody
    ' The custody seed this world signs with for a name: its own, or one it
    ' claimed.
    \ k=desk/keys me=nat name=nat
    ^ nat
    ? (eq name me) k.custody
    | desk/claimed k name
  + root
    ' Where asks are kept.
    \ self=iota
    ^ path
    [self 'io 'mesa 'ask]
  + pending
    ' The asks the foot has not answered.
    \ self=iota state=namespace
    ^ row[[at=path ask=myth]]
    = none=row[[at=path ask=myth]] []
      root (desk/root self)
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (gt record.nat_at(['done] 0) 0) acc
      ? (eq 0 record.txt_at(['want]).len) acc
      | acc.snoc([root.weld(rel) record])
  + used
    ' The asks that are answered and were handed a secret that is still
    ' there: the number each was handed under.
    \ self=iota state=namespace
    ^ row[[at=path handed=nat]]
    = none=row[[at=path handed=nat]] []
      root (desk/root self)
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['done] 0)) acc
      ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['handed] 0)) acc
      ? (gt record.nat_at(['spent] 0) 0) acc
      | acc.snoc([root.weld(rel) record.nat_at(['handed] 0)])
  + mark
    ' An ask answered, with what it is told.
    \ at=path told=myth
    ^ [p=path q=writ]
    [at (writ/poke told.put(['done] (pails/n 1)))]
  + say
    ' A turn that asks the world for these writes, as one event.
    \ writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = plan
        \ now=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        | ./ok writes
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 plan)]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + refuse
    ' An ask that cannot be answered is marked so, and is not tried again.
    \ at=path why=str foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = told=myth (myth/sing ['done] (pails/n 2)).put(['why] (pails/t why))
      writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke told)]]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + mint
    ' An invitation: a name nobody has claimed, founded on a custody key
    ' made from a secret this world derives under the ask's number (id).
    ' The name's card is kept with its founding and its first statement,
    ' which gives the live key to this world until the name is claimed,
    ' and the ask is told the name. dat is what the founding binds.
    \ k=desk/keys at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = id ask.nat_at(['id] 0)
    ? (eq 0 id) (desk/refuse at "an invitation needs a number" foot)
    = made (pass/mint (desk/invitation k id) ask.nat_at(['dat] 0) (Ed25519PublicKey k.live))
      card=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa ($x made.name)]
      log=row[pass/statement] [made.first]
      told (desk/mark at (myth/sing ['name] (pails/n made.name)))
      only=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told]
      plan
        \ now=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        ? (maybe/is_some (pass/held card now)) (./ok only)
        ?> (./ok writes) (pass/meet card made.made log now) (./err 'desk_mint)
        | ./ok writes.snoc(told)
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 plan)]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + claim
    ' The first act of whoever opens an invitation: one statement, signed
    ' with the invitation's secret, that moves the name's custody to a key
    ' of this world's and names this world's live key. secret is what this
    ' world's door was handed; it reaches the foot as a file and is never
    ' a record.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat at=path ask=myth state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = name ask.nat_at(['name] 0)
    ? (lt (wid secret) 2) (desk/refuse at "the invitation's secret was not handed over" foot)
    ? (eq 0 name) (desk/refuse at "a claim names what it claims" foot)
    ? (eq name (mesa_foot/id foot.self)) (desk/claim_self k secret at state foot)
    | desk/claim_name k secret name at ask foot
  + claim_self
    ' A world prepared for a place claims itself: custody becomes its own
    ' custody seed, and the claim is taken onto its own card.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat at=path state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = home (mesa_foot/home foot)
      name (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
    ?> (./some stands) (pass/held home state) (desk/refuse at "this world has no log to claim" foot)
    = s (pass/claim secret name stands (Ed25519PublicKey k.custody) (Ed25519PublicKey k.live))
    ? (either/is_err (pass/next name stands s)) (desk/refuse at "the secret is not this invitation's" foot)
    = told (desk/mark at myth/new)
      plan
        \ now=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        ?> (./ok writes) (pass/turn home s now) (./err 'desk_claim)
        | ./ok writes.snoc(told)
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 plan)]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + claim_name
    ' A world claims a name that is not its own, and keeps the name's log
    ' on a card: the founding (form, custody, dat) and the first statement
    ' (first, as it travels) come with the ask, and are checked against
    ' the name before anything is signed. Custody becomes a key this
    ' world derives for the name.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat name=nat at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = made (pass/founding ask.nat_at(['form] 0) ask.nat_at(['custody] 0) ask.nat_at(['dat] 0))
      card=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa ($x name)]
    ?> (./some first) (pass/got ask.nat_at(['first] 0)) (desk/refuse at "a claim needs the name's first statement" foot)
    = one=row[pass/statement] [first]
    ?> (./ok stands) (pass/read name made one) (desk/refuse at "the founding and first statement are not this name's" foot)
    = s (pass/claim secret name stands (Ed25519PublicKey (desk/claimed k name)) (Ed25519PublicKey k.live))
    ? (either/is_err (pass/next name stands s)) (desk/refuse at "the secret is not this invitation's" foot)
    = log=row[pass/statement] [first s]
      told (desk/mark at myth/new)
      only=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told]
      plan
        \ now=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        ? (maybe/is_some (pass/held card now)) (./ok only)
        ?> (./ok writes) (pass/meet card made log now) (./err 'desk_claim)
        | ./ok writes.snoc(told)
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 plan)]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + bring
    ' This world is brought before another (to) by a name (by: itself when
    ' the ask names none, or an invitation it claimed), at an address. The
    ' introduction is signed by the custody this world holds for that name
    ' and by its own custody, and is kept on this world's card for the
    ' other in the slot bring, from where the foot says it on every tick.
    \ k=desk/keys at=path ask=myth state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      home (mesa_foot/home foot)
      to ask.nat_at(['to] 0)
      by (? (eq 0 ask.nat_at(['by] 0)) me ask.nat_at(['by] 0))
      port ask.nat_at(['port] 0)
      peer=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa ($x to)]
    ? (eq 0 to) (desk/refuse at "an introduction is to a world" foot)
    ? (eq 0 port) (desk/refuse at "an introduction says where the world is reached" foot)
    ?> (./some made) (pass/founded home state) (desk/refuse at "this world has no founding" foot)
    ?> (./some stands) (pass/held home state) (desk/refuse at "this world has stated no key" foot)
    ? !(net/live peer state) (desk/refuse at "this world keeps no card for that world" foot)
    = letter (pass/letter (pass/introduce (desk/custody k me by) k.custody to by me made stands ask.txt_at(['host]) port))
      writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[peer (writ/poke (myth/sing ['bring] (pails/n letter)))] (desk/mark at myth/new)]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + grant
    ' Leave to act at a door, for a session: signed by the custody this
    ' world holds for the name (its own when the ask names none), and told
    ' to the ask. The session is the hash of a secret this world never
    ' sees.
    \ k=desk/keys at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      name (? (eq 0 ask.nat_at(['name] 0)) me ask.nat_at(['name] 0))
      session ask.nat_at(['session] 0)
      until ask.nat_at(['until] 0)
    ? (eq 0 session) (desk/refuse at "a grant is for a session" foot)
    ? (eq 0 until) (desk/refuse at "a grant ends" foot)
    = g (pass/allow (desk/custody k me name) name session until)
      told (desk/mark at (myth/sing ['sig] (pails/n g.sig)).put(['name] (pails/n name)))
      writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [told]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + link
    ' The secret of an invitation, for whoever is to be given its link.
    ' It is not told to the ask. The foot leaves it as a file in
    ' io/mesa/out under the invitation's number, where this world's door
    ' takes it once; here the ask is only marked.
    \ at=path ask=myth foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    ? (eq 0 ask.nat_at(['id] 0)) (desk/refuse at "a link is to an invitation's number" foot)
    = writes=row[[p=path q=writ]] [(desk/mark at myth/new)]
    | desk/say writes foot
  + answer
    ' One ask, answered. secret is what the ask was handed, or nothing.
    \ k=desk/keys secret=nat at=path ask=myth state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = want ask.txt_at(['want])
    ? (equal[str] want "mint") (desk/mint k at ask foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "claim") (desk/claim k secret at ask state foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "bring") (desk/bring k at ask state foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "grant") (desk/grant k at ask foot)
    ? (equal[str] want "link") (desk/link at ask foot)
    | desk/refuse at "the desk does not know this ask" foot
